O king, you are my worshipful guest. I was thinking of you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-76-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7067009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b6b28fbc47ebaf798ba3501cc93a3a2c1e5d3c42887c533911c80957fb9a9f0c","compact":"8ea12aa1ed5806d2b33c29679d8731a696eb27a1813728d089d6123bc05fda6c","nasal":"8ea12aa1ed5806d2b33c29679d8731a696eb27a1813728d089d6123bc05fda6c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-67-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":67,"verse":10,"english":"The celestials informed me that you went coming having slain the Sūdra ascetic. You have observed piety and have given back life to dead child of the Brahmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-76-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7067010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"113ccdde8252764a728fefc7a0031e7535742c0380b8c88176e2fe543166f8fa","compact":"9ce8d3488062d9830839ed58e8b17fb94d24cf5749a9cd9cb57b322d7926ff95","nasal":"c6d18161a3676a6603cec32b5edcf583eddbf7c6a00a66fd827d50d6f361e0df"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-67-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":67,"verse":11,"english":"Do you spend this night with me, O Rāghava. You are the graceful Nārāyaṇa. In you the whole universe is established. You are the lord of all creatures and the eternal Purusha. You shall go to your city next morning in your Pușpaka car.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.87,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-76-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7067011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9ec6cf7a1405b9f9cb0e43d5dbd963bd0e6f9f4869f2d72656164b392213c30e","compact":"e291d64967b47878dfd2e4f433e506164e6571921683df6c7b70b7738f5722