a":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":67,"verse":14,"english":"Therefore, O Rama, by virtue of Indra's portion, do you accept this omament and confer upon me the salvation. Hearing the words of the Muni, Rāma took from him that brilliant celestial ornament burning like the rays of the Sun. And having taken that excellent ornament, Dāsarathi asked the great saint Kumbhayoni, saying.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-76-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7067014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ee25b98d55cc17a4b527a36ec5fbc653fb6b3be2a02bbc1b3cc9642185cc0a6","compact":"e18f1333a87a7719b759d3106161473267f90d76a47cc9ad6b70644eaeb5abb3","nasal":"e18f1333a87a7719b759d3106161473267f90d76a47cc9ad6b70644eaeb5abb3"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-67-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":67,"verse":15,"english":"Therefore, O Rama, by virtue of Indra's portion, do you accept this omament and confer upon me the salvation. Hearing the words of the Muni, Rāma took from him that brilliant celestial ornament burning like the rays of the Sun. And having taken that excellent ornament, Dāsarathi asked the great saint Kumbhayoni, saying.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-76-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7067015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"60a3bd3b79623326a6d3ee6e96c27fb9d8449c525346ba1a604da0c32b235ff5","compact":"0dc2b41e19c781ec95b75de9a13510e60dc93cf623ca5537a7bb117483fed27d","nasal":"0dc2b41e19c781ec95b75de9a13510e60dc93cf623ca5537a7bb117483fed27d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-67-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":67,"verse":16,"english":"When have you obtained this celestial ornamens of a wondrous make? Who have given you this? O Brāhmaṇa, I do accost you thus out of curiosity. You are 